One subtle point in the bridge audit is worth making explicit: the generated theorem is abstract enough that deliberately constant parameter definitions can satisfy it. I verified that counterfactual in Lean, then checked the actual 15 candidate definitions against the bound K symbols and the source-reachable supplied-semantics cases; the actual definitions implement the relevant dispatches and are distinguished by negative, mixed-type, and parity examples.
